<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      Stopgap only. Raising targetSdk to 35 (commit a804357) made Android 15
      force edge-to-edge, so the WebView is drawn underneath the status bar and
      the system bar swallows touches in that band: Facebook's own header back
      arrow and search icon stay visible but become untappable.

      This attribute restores the pre-API-35 behaviour of giving the system bars
      their own space. It is DEPRECATED and is only honoured up to targetSdk 35 -
      it will be ignored in a future release, so this is not a long-term fix.

      It lives in values-v35/ because it requires API 35 and minSdk is 26. On
      API 26-34 edge-to-edge was never forced and the base theme is already
      correct, so those versions keep the plain Theme.SlimBook.

      TODO: replace with real inset handling (fitsSystemWindows on the root
      FrameLayout, or ViewCompat.setOnApplyWindowInsetsListener applying
      systemBars() insets), keeping statsBadge and messengerButton inside the
      inset-safe area so they do not end up under the status bar instead.
      Tracked in issue #20.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.SlimBook" parent="Theme.AppCompat.Light.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowOptOutEdgeToEdgeEnforcement">true</item>
    </style>
</resources>
